From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0000
Subject: wireless: uwe5622: unlink an interface before freeing it

Unisoc's later sprdwl driver (sc2355/merlion) already does this.

sprdwl_cfg80211_del_iface() frees the vif in sprdwl_del_iface() and then
list_del()s it. For a P2P device (wpa_supplicant's p2p-dev-wlan0) the vif
is kfree()d at once:

  BUG: KASAN: slab-use-after-free in sprdwl_cfg80211_del_iface+0x23c/0x280 [sprdwl_ng]
  Freed by task 758:
   kfree+0x24c/0x490
   sprdwl_del_iface+0x12c/0x1c0 [sprdwl_ng]
   sprdwl_cfg80211_del_iface+0x128/0x280 [sprdwl_ng]

Unlink it under the list lock first, as sprdwl_del_all_ifaces() does.
An unknown wdev no longer reaches sprdwl_del_iface() with the list head.

Upstream: to be submitted to https://github.com/armbian/uwe5622
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwifi/cfg80211.c | 19 +++++++------------
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwifi/cfg80211.c b/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwifi/cfg80211.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwifi/cfg80211.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwifi/cfg80211.c
@@ -581,27 +581,22 @@ static int sprdwl_cfg80211_del_iface(str
 				     struct wireless_dev *wdev)
 {
 	struct sprdwl_priv *priv = wiphy_priv(wiphy);
-	struct sprdwl_vif *vif = NULL, *tmp_vif = NULL;
+	struct sprdwl_vif *vif;
 
 	if (sprdwl_intf_is_exit(priv)) {
 		wiphy_err(wiphy, "%s driver removing!\n", __func__);
 		return 0;
 	}
 	spin_lock_bh(&priv->list_lock);
-	list_for_each_entry_safe(vif, tmp_vif, &priv->vif_list, vif_node) {
-		if (&vif->wdev == wdev)
-			break;
+	list_for_each_entry(vif, &priv->vif_list, vif_node) {
+		if (&vif->wdev == wdev) {
+			list_del(&vif->vif_node);
+			spin_unlock_bh(&priv->list_lock);
+			return sprdwl_del_iface(priv, vif);
+		}
 	}
 	spin_unlock_bh(&priv->list_lock);
 
-	if (vif != NULL) {
-		sprdwl_del_iface(priv, vif);
-
-		spin_lock_bh(&priv->list_lock);
-		list_del(&vif->vif_node);
-		spin_unlock_bh(&priv->list_lock);
-	}
-
 	return 0;
 }
 
